WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:02.880
Mind Your Decisions, I'm Presh Talwalkar.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:08.060
Rectangle ABCD is divided into smaller rectangles.

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:12.740
All of the dimensions in this diagram are given in centimeters

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:15.580
and the diagram is not drawn to scale.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:20.120
The shaded rectangle has an area of 9 cm².

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:23.620
Find the area of rectangle ABCD.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:27.700
Pause the video if you'd like to give this problem a try,

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:31.400
and when you're ready, keep watching to learn how to solve this problem.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:44.000
[Music]

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.160
We'll get started by focusing on the dimensions of the shaded rectangle.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:51.420
We then calculate the area of this rectangle.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.200
It'll be y(y - 8).

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.040
This is equal to 9 cm².

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:02.460
We then distribute the Y term and subtract 9 from both sides.

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:07.460
We factor the quadratic equation, and we get two potential solutions,

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:10.320
y is equal to 9, and y is equal to -1.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:13.700
Since we're dealing with lengths, we want a positive value,

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:15.740
so we retain y is equal to 9.

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:19.580
We then calculate the length of AD.

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:23.980
It'll be equal to (1 + 11).

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:27.340
The total length will be equal to 12,

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:32.220
and that's the length of BC because opposite sides in a rectangle have the same length.

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:35.110
We then have x is equal to 12.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:41.830
The length of AB is equal to (x - 4), which means AV is equal to 8.

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:46.900
So it seems like we can calculate the area of ABCD as follows:

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:51.880
It's equal to 8 times 12, which is equal to 96 cm².

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:56.420
This would seem to be the answer, but it's not correct.

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:00.360
Go back to the original diagram and notice

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:03.460
that a portion of CD is equal to y,

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:07.460
which means a portion of CD is equal to 9.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.620
So we have a very strange shape.

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:13.520
The entire length of AB is equal to 8,

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:16.580
but its opposite side, which is supposed to be equal to 8,

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:19.040
has a portion which is equal to 9.

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:23.020
In other words, we have a portion of a side being

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:24.610
longer than the side itself.

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:29.820
So the actual answer is we cannot calculate the area of ABCD

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:33.560
because the dimensions in this problem are impossible.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:37.940
After the test was given, they did admit this was an error in the exam.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:42.280
Personally, I'm not opposed to trick questions once in a while

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:45.440
because it keeps students on guard from broke calculations.

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:50.600
So always be careful if the dimensions actually make any sense.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:55.760
Thanks for making MindYourDecisions one of the best channel on YouTube.

00:02:55.760 --> 00:03:00.280
As always, thanks for watching and thanks for your support.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:12.720
[Music]

